{"tool_name":"phigaro","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"phigaro","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btaa250"],"license":"Not available","summary":"Phigaro is a scalable command-line tool for predicting phages and prophages.","home_url":"https://phigaro.readthedocs.io/","keywords":["High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Metagenome","Metagenomics","Prophages"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":1192},"biotools":{"id":"phigaro","home":"https://github.com/bobeobibo/phigaro","license":"MIT","summary":"Phigaro is a high-throughput prophage sequence annotation.\n\nPhigaro is a standalone command-line application that is able to detect prophage regions taking raw genome and metagenome assemblies as an input. It also produces dynamic annotated \u201cprophage genome maps\u201d and marks possible transposon insertion spots inside prophages. It is applicable for mining prophage regions from large metagenomic datasets.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T08:43:09Z","last_update_date":"2021-01-23T15:07:40Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:phigaro","credit":[{"email":"estarikova@rcpcm.org","name":"Elizaveta V Starikova","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genome annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0362"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2429"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"Phigaro","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTAA250","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020 The Author(s) 2020. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved. For permissions, please e-mail: journals.permissions@oup.com. Phigaro is a standalone command-line application that is able to detect prophage regions taking raw genome and metagenome assemblies as an input. It also produces dynamic annotated 'prophage genome maps' and marks possible transposo